From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ssh: give the FallbackPort attempt a full ConnectTimeout

After a timed out connect to the default port the client tries FallbackPort, but
passed on the time that was left of ConnectTimeout, which is 0 once it has run
out. OpenSSH's waitrfd() now treats a timeout of 0 or less as no limit, so on
a base that has that change the second attempt waited for as long as the system
allows. Reset the time to the whole ConnectTimeout before the retry.
---
 ssh.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ssh.c b/ssh.c
index 7e8d72d90..08c18ca99 100644
--- a/ssh.c
+++ b/ssh.c
@@ -1763,6 +1763,15 @@ tryagain:
 				freeaddrinfo(addrs);
 			addrs = resolve_host(host, port, 1,
 					     cname, sizeof(cname));
+			/*
+			 * The first attempt left the time that remained of
+			 * ConnectTimeout in timeout_ms, which is 0 once it ran
+			 * out, and 0 means no limit: give this one a full turn.
+			 */
+			if (options.connection_timeout >= INT_MAX/1000)
+				timeout_ms = INT_MAX;
+			else
+				timeout_ms = options.connection_timeout * 1000;
 			goto tryagain;
 		} else {
 			exit(255);
-- 
